{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1569909368,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDA2Nzk2Nzk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3738","origin":"github"},"title":"Remove UI support functionality from Repo classes","message":"The most intrusive thing in this category is low-level code trying to figure out how many files to `get` in order to render proper progress bars. Given that in many cases (now) high-level code has executed `status()` or some of its lower-level helpers, this information is likely to be present already, and duplication in low-level code is just slowing things down (and also needlessly complicating the logic).\n\nI believe that we should RF this to just yield the relevant progress log messages, which can either be ignored by a caller, or put to use in a progress bar that is properly configured by the caller already.","files":null}]}